  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find separator rows/cols (all 4s)\n    sep_rows = [r for r in range(rows) if all(grid[r][c] == 4 for c in range(cols))]\n    sep_cols = [c for c in range(cols) if all(grid[r][c] == 4 for r in range(rows))]\n    \n    # Build row/col boundaries\n    r_bounds = [-1] + sep_rows + [rows]\n    c_bounds = [-1] + sep_cols + [cols]\n    \n    regions = []\n    source = None\n    for i in range(len(r_bounds)-1):\n        for j in range(len(c_bounds)-1):\n            r1, r2 = r_bounds[i]+1, r_bounds[i+1]\n            c1, c2 = c_bounds[j]+1, c_bounds[j+1]\n            has_content = any(grid[r][c] != 0 for r in range(r1,r2) for c in range(c1,c2))\n            regions.append((r1,r2,c1,c2,has_content))\n            if has_content:\n                source = (r1,r2,c1,c2)\n    \n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    sr1,sr2,sc1,sc2 = source\n    for r1,r2,c1,c2,has in regions:\n        if not has:\n            for r in range(r2-r1):\n                for c in range(c2-c1):\n                    result[r1+r][c1+c] = grid[sr1+r][sc1+c]\n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find separator rows/cols (all 4s)\n    sep_rows = [r for r in range(rows) if all(grid[r][c] == 4 for c in range(cols))]\n    sep_cols = [c for c in range(cols) if all(grid[r][c] == 4 for r in range(rows))]\n    \n    # Build row/col boundaries\n    r_bounds = [-1] + sep_rows + [rows]\n    c_bounds = [-1] + sep_cols + [cols]\n    \n    regions = []\n    source = None\n    for i in range(len(r_bounds)-1):\n        for j in range(len(c_bounds)-1):\n            r1, r2 = r_bounds[i]+1, r_bounds[i+1]\n            c1, c2 = c_bounds[j]+1, c_bounds[j+1]\n            has_content = any(grid[r][c] != 0 for r in range(r1,r2) for c in range(c1,c2))\n            regions.append((r1,r2,c1,c2,has_content))\n            if has_content:\n                source = (r1,r2,c1,c2)\n    \n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    sr1,sr2,sc1,sc2 = source\n    for r1,r2,c1,c2,has in regions:\n        if not has:\n            for r in range(r2-r1):\n                for c in range(c2-c1):\n                    result[r1+r][c1+c] = grid[sr1+r][sc1+c]\n    return result",
